VG.registerBibleChapters("genesis", [
{n:21, name:"Isaac Is Born", seal:{ref:"Genesis 21:12",verse:"And God said unto Abraham, Let it not be grievous in thy sight because of the lad, and because of thy bondwoman; in all that Sarah hath said unto thee, hearken unto her voice; for in Isaac shall thy seed be called."}, facts:["Did you know the name Isaac means 'he laughs'? God named the child of promise after Sarah's laugh, turning her doubt into joy (Genesis 21:6).","Did you know Abraham was a hundred years old when Isaac was born? The promise waited until every human possibility was gone (Genesis 21:5).","Did you know Beersheba means 'well of the oath'? Abraham and Abimelech swore their covenant there beside the well Abraham had dug (Genesis 21:31)."], questions:[
{q:"What did Abraham name the son Sarah bore to him?",options:["Isaac","Ishmael","Jacob","Esau"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 21:3",verse:"And Abraham called the name of his son that was born unto him, whom Sarah bare to him, Isaac.",insight:"Isaac means 'he laughs.' God took Sarah's doubting laugh and turned it into the child's name, so every time she called him she remembered joy."},
{q:"How old was Abraham when Isaac was born to him?",options:["A hundred years old","Eighty years old","Ninety years old","Seventy five years old"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 21:5",verse:"And Abraham was an hundred years old, when his son Isaac was born unto him.",insight:"A hundred years old, well past hoping. God's promises do not expire with our strength; they arrive right on His schedule."},
{q:"At what age did Abraham circumcise Isaac?",options:["Eight days old","Thirty days old","One year old","Forty days old"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 21:4",verse:"And Abraham circumcised his son Isaac being eight days old, as God had commanded him.",insight:"On the eighth day, exactly as God had commanded. Joy never cancelled obedience; Abraham celebrated the promise and kept the covenant in the same week."},
{q:"What did Sarah say God had made her to do?",options:["Laugh","Weep","Sing","Dance"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 21:6",verse:"And Sarah said, God hath made me to laugh, so that all that hear will laugh with me.",insight:"God hath made me to laugh, so that all that hear will laugh with me. The laugh of disbelief in the tent became the laugh of delight in her arms."},
{q:"On what occasion did Abraham make a great feast?",options:["The same day Isaac was weaned","The day Isaac was born","The day Isaac was circumcised","The day Isaac turned thirteen"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 21:8",verse:"And the child grew, and was weaned: and Abraham made a great feast the same day that Isaac was weaned.",insight:"When the child was weaned, Abraham feasted. Mark the milestones of God's faithfulness; gratitude loves a table."},
{q:"Whom did Sarah see mocking?",options:["The son of Hagar the Egyptian","The son of Lot","The son of Abimelech","A Philistine boy"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 21:9",verse:"And Sarah saw the son of Hagar the Egyptian, which she had born unto Abraham, mocking.",insight:"Ishmael's mocking stung because it touched the promise itself. Sarah saw what Abraham had to learn: the flesh always mocks the promise until God settles it."},
{q:"What did Sarah demand Abraham do with Hagar and her son?",options:["Cast out the bondwoman and her son","Send them to Egypt in honor","Make Ishmael the heir","Build them a house in Hebron"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 21:10",verse:"Wherefore she said unto Abraham, Cast out this bondwoman and her son: for the son of this bondwoman shall not be heir with my son, even with Isaac.",insight:"Her words were harsh, yet God confirmed the heart of them: the inheritance would run through Isaac. God's purposes stand even when our handling of them is rough."},
{q:"How did Abraham feel about sending Hagar and Ishmael away?",options:["The thing was very grievous in his sight","He was glad to be rid of them","He felt nothing at all","He laughed at Sarah's demand"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 21:11",verse:"And the thing was very grievous in Abraham’s sight because of his son.",insight:"It was very grievous in his sight because of his son. Obedience can still break the heart, and God did not rebuke Abraham for grieving; He guided him through it."},
{q:"What promise did God make concerning Ishmael?",options:["He would make a nation of him, because he was Abraham's seed","He would bring him back to Egypt","He would make him king of Canaan","He would give him Isaac's inheritance"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 21:13",verse:"And also of the son of the bondwoman will I make a nation, because he is thy seed.",insight:"God's care reached beyond the chosen line. Ishmael was not the child of promise, but he was still Abraham's seed, and God made him a nation too."},
{q:"What did Abraham give Hagar when he sent her away?",options:["Bread and a bottle of water","Silver and gold","A tent and livestock","Nothing at all"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 21:14",verse:"And Abraham rose up early in the morning, and took bread, and a bottle of water, and gave it unto Hagar, putting it on her shoulder, and the child, and sent her away: and she departed, and wandered in the wilderness of Beer-sheba.",insight:"Bread and water on her shoulder, given at dawn. Human provision runs out in the wilderness, which is exactly where God's provision begins."},
{q:"What did Hagar do when the water in the bottle was spent?",options:["She cast the child under one of the shrubs","She dug a well with her hands","She walked back to Abraham","She left the child and fled"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 21:15",verse:"And the water was spent in the bottle, and she cast the child under one of the shrubs.",insight:"She laid him under a shrub, out of things to try. Despair is often the doorway; God was already listening before she lifted her voice."},
{q:"How far from Ishmael did Hagar sit down to weep?",options:["As it were a bowshot","A Sabbath day's journey","A stone's throw","A hundred paces"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 21:16",verse:"And she went, and sat her down over against him a good way off, as it were a bowshot: for she said, Let me not see the death of the child. And she sat over against him, and lift up her voice, and wept.",insight:"A bowshot away, close enough to love him, too far to watch him die. A mother's grief sat down in the sand, and heaven leaned in."},
{q:"What did the angel of God say to Hagar out of heaven?",options:["What aileth thee, Hagar? fear not","Return to Sarah at once","Go back to the land of Egypt","Dig here and you will find water"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 21:17",verse:"And God heard the voice of the lad; and the angel of God called Hagar out of heaven, and said unto her, What aileth thee, Hagar? fear not; for God hath heard the voice of the lad where he is.",insight:"God heard the voice of the lad where he was. Notice: the boy was too weak to cry out, yet God heard. He hears us in our weakest places."},
{q:"What did God open Hagar's eyes to see?",options:["A well of water","A caravan of merchants","An angel with a sword","A city in the distance"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 21:19",verse:"And God opened her eyes, and she saw a well of water; and she went, and filled the bottle with water, and gave the lad drink.",insight:"The well was there all along; she needed opened eyes to see it. So much of God's provision is near us already, waiting for Him to open our sight."},
{q:"What skill did Ishmael develop as he grew in the wilderness?",options:["He became an archer","He became a shepherd","He became a scribe","He became a tentmaker"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 21:20",verse:"And God was with the lad; and he grew, and dwelt in the wilderness, and became an archer.",insight:"God was with the lad, and he grew strong with a bow in his hand. Gifts can grow in hard places when God is with the growing."},
{q:"From where did Hagar take a wife for Ishmael?",options:["Out of the land of Egypt","Out of the land of Canaan","Out of Haran","Out of Gerar"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 21:21",verse:"And he dwelt in the wilderness of Paran: and his mother took him a wife out of the land of Egypt.",insight:"Out of Egypt, her own homeland. Even in exile, roots remember themselves; God lets us carry home with us."},
{q:"Who came to Abraham saying, God is with thee in all that thou doest?",options:["Abimelech and Phichol","The king of Sodom","Melchizedek","Pharaoh's captain"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 21:22",verse:"And it came to pass at that time, that Abimelech and Phichol the chief captain of his host spake unto Abraham, saying, God is with thee in all that thou doest:",insight:"A pagan king and his captain saw it plainly. A life walked with God becomes visible; watching neighbors notice before we do."},
{q:"How many ewe lambs did Abraham set apart as a witness about the well?",options:["Seven","Three","Ten","Twelve"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 21:28",verse:"And Abraham set seven ewe lambs of the flock by themselves.",insight:"Seven lambs set by themselves, a living receipt. Abraham sealed his claim with evidence, keeping both his well and his peace."},
{q:"What did Abraham ask Abimelech to take as a witness that he had dug the well?",options:["The seven ewe lambs","A bag of silver","A young bull","A woven cloak"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 21:30",verse:"And he said, For these seven ewe lambs shalt thou take of my hand, that they may be a witness unto me, that I have digged this well.",insight:"Take these of my hand, that they may be a witness unto me. Truth kept with evidence and peace kept with honor; Abraham held both."},
{q:"What did Abraham plant at Beersheba, and whom did he call upon there?",options:["A grove, and the LORD, the everlasting God","A vineyard, and the God of his fathers","An olive tree, and El Shaddai","A garden, and the angel of the LORD"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 21:33",verse:"And Abraham planted a grove in Beer-sheba, and called there on the name of the LORD, the everlasting God.",insight:"He planted a grove, a slow growing thing, and called on the everlasting God. Worship planted like a tree outlasts the planter."}
]},
{n:22, name:"The Offering on Moriah", seal:{ref:"Genesis 22:14",verse:"And Abraham called the name of that place Jehovah-jireh: as it is said to this day, In the mount of the LORD it shall be seen."}, facts:["Did you know Abraham's journey to Moriah took three days? Three days of walking with the promise in one hand and the command in the other (Genesis 22:4).","Did you know Solomon later built the temple on Mount Moriah? The hillside of Abraham's altar became the place of Israel's worship (2 Chronicles 3:1).","Did you know Jehovahjireh means 'the LORD will provide'? Abraham named the mountain after God's provision, and the name became a proverb (Genesis 22:14)."], questions:[
{q:"How does the chapter describe God's command to Abraham?",options:["God did tempt, that is, test, Abraham","God did punish Abraham","God did abandon Abraham","God did reward Abraham"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 22:1",verse:"And it came to pass after these things, that God did tempt Abraham, and said unto him, Abraham: and he said, Behold, here I am.",insight:"God tested Abraham; He never tempts toward evil. Testing proves faith the way fire proves gold, and Abraham answered, Here I am."},
{q:"Where did God tell Abraham to offer Isaac?",options:["The land of Moriah","The plains of Mamre","Mount Sinai","The land of Egypt"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 22:2",verse:"And he said, Take now thy son, thine only son Isaac, whom thou lovest, and get thee into the land of Moriah; and offer him there for a burnt offering upon one of the mountains which I will tell thee of.",insight:"Take now thy son, thine only son Isaac, whom thou lovest. God named every tender tie, then said, go. Obedience often walks before understanding."},
{q:"Who went with Abraham and Isaac toward Moriah?",options:["Two of his young men, with his ass","Sarah and her maid","Three angels","No one at all"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 22:3",verse:"And Abraham rose up early in the morning, and saddled his ass, and took two of his young men with him, and Isaac his son, and clave the wood for the burnt offering, and rose up, and went unto the place of which God had told him.",insight:"He rose up early, saddled his ass, and clave the wood himself. Great obedience is quiet and early; it does not wait to feel ready."},
{q:"On which day did Abraham lift up his eyes and see the place afar off?",options:["The third day","The seventh day","The fortieth day","The first day"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 22:4",verse:"Then on the third day Abraham lifted up his eyes, and saw the place afar off.",insight:"Three days of walking with the promise and the pain side by side. Faith kept walking when every step must have argued for turning back."},
{q:"What did Abraham tell the young men he and Isaac would do?",options:["Go yonder and worship, and come again to you","Build a city and return","Hunt game and return","Offer a lamb and come again"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 22:5",verse:"And Abraham said unto his young men, Abide ye here with the ass; and I and the lad will go yonder and worship, and come again to you,",insight:"I and the lad will go yonder and worship, and come again to you. He spoke of both returning; faith was already reaching for resurrection."},
{q:"What did Isaac carry up the mountain?",options:["The wood for the burnt offering","The knife","The fire in his hand","The stones for the altar"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 22:6",verse:"And Abraham took the wood of the burnt offering, and laid it upon Isaac his son; and he took the fire in his hand, and a knife; and they went both of them together.",insight:"Abraham laid the wood upon Isaac his son. The son bearing the wood up Moriah foreshadows the greater Son bearing His cross up Calvary."},
{q:"What question did Isaac ask his father on the way?",options:["Behold the fire and the wood, but where is the lamb for a burnt offering","Why have we come so far","Will God accept our worship","Where are the young men"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 22:7",verse:"And Isaac spake unto Abraham his father, and said, My father: and he said, Here am I, my son. And he said, Behold the fire and the wood: but where is the lamb for a burnt offering?",insight:"An honest question from a trusting son. Isaac noticed the missing lamb, and his father answered with the gospel in a sentence."},
{q:"How did Abraham answer Isaac about the lamb?",options:["My son, God will provide himself a lamb for a burnt offering","We will buy one in the city below","The young men are bringing one","We need no lamb today"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 22:8",verse:"And Abraham said, My son, God will provide himself a lamb for a burnt offering: so they went both of them together.",insight:"God will provide himself a lamb. Spoken on Moriah, fulfilled on Calvary: God did provide Himself the Lamb."},
{q:"What did Abraham do to Isaac at the altar?",options:["He bound him and laid him on the altar upon the wood","He anointed him with oil","He set him beside the altar","He sent him back down the mountain"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 22:9",verse:"And they came to the place which God had told him of; and Abraham built an altar there, and laid the wood in order, and bound Isaac his son, and laid him on the altar upon the wood.",insight:"He bound Isaac his son. Notice Isaac's trust too; the strong young man let his aged father bind him. Surrender ran in the family."},
{q:"What stopped Abraham's hand as he stretched it out with the knife?",options:["The angel of the LORD calling out of heaven","Sarah crying out from below","The ram breaking free","The young men running up"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 22:11",verse:"And the angel of the LORD called unto him out of heaven, and said, Abraham, Abraham: and he said, Here am I.",insight:"Abraham, Abraham, called out of heaven, twice named, fully stopped. God interrupts our hardest obediences with mercy at the last possible moment."},
{q:"What did the angel say God now knew about Abraham?",options:["That he feared God, since he had not withheld his son","That he loved Isaac more than God","That he doubted the promise","That he feared man more than God"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 22:12",verse:"And he said, Lay not thine hand upon the lad, neither do thou any thing unto him: for now I know that thou fearest God, seeing thou hast not withheld thy son, thine only son from me.",insight:"Now I know that thou fearest God. Reverent fear is proved not by feelings but by surrender; Abraham held nothing back, so God held nothing back."},
{q:"What did Abraham see caught in the thicket?",options:["A ram caught by his horns","A lamb caught by its leg","A goat tangled in vines","A young bull stuck fast"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 22:13",verse:"And Abraham lifted up his eyes, and looked, and behold behind him a ram caught in a thicket by his horns: and Abraham went and took the ram, and offered him up for a burnt offering in the stead of his son.",insight:"Behind him a ram caught in a thicket by his horns. God's substitute was already there, waiting to be seen; provision often arrives before we look up."},
{q:"What did Abraham offer in the stead of his son?",options:["The ram from the thicket","A turtledove","A young bullock","Nothing, he went home"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 22:13",verse:"And Abraham lifted up his eyes, and looked, and behold behind him a ram caught in a thicket by his horns: and Abraham went and took the ram, and offered him up for a burnt offering in the stead of his son.",insight:"He offered up the ram for a burnt offering in the stead of his son. Substitution, the heart of the gospel, acted out on Moriah centuries before Calvary."},
{q:"What name did Abraham give to the place?",options:["Jehovahjireh","Bethel","Peniel","Ebenezer"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 22:14",verse:"And Abraham called the name of that place Jehovah-jireh: as it is said to this day, In the mount of the LORD it shall be seen.",insight:"Jehovahjireh, the LORD will provide, or the LORD will see. Abraham named the mountain as a memorial, so every traveler after him would remember."},
{q:"What saying arose from that place?",options:["In the mount of the LORD it shall be seen","The LORD is my shepherd","Great is His faithfulness","Blessed be the name of the LORD"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 22:14",verse:"And Abraham called the name of that place Jehovah-jireh: as it is said to this day, In the mount of the LORD it shall be seen.",insight:"In the mount of the LORD it shall be seen. Altars give birth to proverbs; what God did for Abraham became hope for everyone who heard it."},
{q:"By what did the LORD swear His oath to Abraham?",options:["By Himself","By the angels","By the stars","By the covenant"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 22:16",verse:"And said, By myself have I sworn, saith the LORD, for because thou hast done this thing, and hast not withheld thy son, thine only son:",insight:"By myself have I sworn, saith the LORD. There is no greater name to swear by; the promise rests on God's own being and cannot break."},
{q:"To what did God compare the multitude of Abraham's seed?",options:["The stars of heaven and the sand upon the sea shore","The dust of the earth and the drops of rain","The trees of the forest and the fish of the sea","The flocks of the field and the birds of the air"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 22:17",verse:"That in blessing I will bless thee, and in multiplying I will multiply thy seed as the stars of the heaven, and as the sand which is upon the sea shore; and thy seed shall possess the gate of his enemies;",insight:"Stars and sand, the uncountable counted by grace. From one old man would come a multitude no census could hold."},
{q:"Why would all the nations of the earth be blessed in Abraham's seed?",options:["Because Abraham had obeyed God's voice","Because Isaac was the firstborn","Because of the ram in the thicket","Because Abraham was wealthy"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 22:18",verse:"And in thy seed shall all the nations of the earth be blessed; because thou hast obeyed my voice.",insight:"Because thou hast obeyed my voice. Blessing flowed through obedience, and the Seed is Christ, in whom every nation finds blessing."},
{q:"Where did Abraham dwell after returning from Moriah?",options:["At Beersheba","At Hebron","At Bethel","In the land of Egypt"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 22:19",verse:"So Abraham returned unto his young men, and they rose up and went together to Beer-sheba; and Abraham dwelt at Beer-sheba.",insight:"They went together to Beersheba, and Abraham dwelt there. After the mountain, ordinary life by the well of the oath; faith comes home and keeps living."},
{q:"Whose birth was reported to Abraham after these things?",options:["Rebekah, the daughter of Bethuel","Leah, the daughter of Laban","Rachel, the daughter of Laban","Milcah, the wife of Nahor"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 22:23",verse:"And Bethuel begat Rebekah: these eight Milcah did bear to Nahor, Abraham’s brother.",insight:"Bethuel begat Rebekah. While Abraham worshiped on Moriah, God was quietly preparing Isaac's bride far away in Haran. Providence works on both ends at once."}
]},
{n:23, name:"The Cave of Machpelah", seal:{ref:"Genesis 23:19",verse:"And after this, Abraham buried Sarah his wife in the cave of the field of Machpelah before Mamre: the same is Hebron in the land of Canaan."}, facts:["Did you know Sarah is the only woman in the Bible whose age at death is recorded? One hundred and twenty seven years, every one of them counted by God (Genesis 23:1).","Did you know Abraham paid four hundred shekels of silver for the cave? It is one of the earliest land purchases recorded in Scripture, paid in current money with the merchant (Genesis 23:16).","Did you know the cave of Machpelah became the tomb of the patriarchs? Abraham, Sarah, Isaac, Rebekah, Jacob, and Leah were all buried there (Genesis 49:31)."], questions:[
{q:"How old was Sarah when she died?",options:["A hundred and twenty seven years old","A hundred and twenty years old","Ninety years old","A hundred and thirty years old"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 23:1",verse:"And Sarah was an hundred and seven and twenty years old: these were the years of the life of Sarah.",insight:"These were the years of the life of Sarah, all 127 of them. God counts our days, and a life of faith is worth recording to the year."},
{q:"Where did Sarah die?",options:["In Kirjatharba, that is Hebron, in the land of Canaan","In Beersheba","In Haran","In the land of Egypt"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 23:2",verse:"And Sarah died in Kirjath-arba; the same is Hebron in the land of Canaan: and Abraham came to mourn for Sarah, and to weep for her.",insight:"In the land of Canaan, the promised land not yet possessed, yet already home. Faith can die at home in a place it never fully owned."},
{q:"What did Abraham do when Sarah died?",options:["He came to mourn for Sarah, and to weep for her","He immediately bought the field","He returned to Haran","He sent for Isaac"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 23:2",verse:"And Sarah died in Kirjath-arba; the same is Hebron in the land of Canaan: and Abraham came to mourn for Sarah, and to weep for her.",insight:"He came to mourn and to weep. Even the father of faith wept openly; grief is not unbelief, it is love with nowhere to go."},
{q:"How did Abraham describe himself to the sons of Heth?",options:["A stranger and a sojourner","A mighty prince","A wealthy merchant","A citizen of Hebron"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 23:4",verse:"I am a stranger and a sojourner with you: give me a possession of a buryingplace with you, that I may bury my dead out of my sight.",insight:"I am a stranger and a sojourner with you. He owned flocks and silver, yet held the world loosely; his citizenship was in the promise."},
{q:"What did Abraham ask the sons of Heth to give him?",options:["A possession of a buryingplace","A field for his flocks","A house in the city","A well of water"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 23:4",verse:"I am a stranger and a sojourner with you: give me a possession of a buryingplace with you, that I may bury my dead out of my sight.",insight:"A possession of a buryingplace. His first owned soil in Canaan would be a grave; hope beyond death anchored him to the land."},
{q:"What did the children of Heth call Abraham?",options:["A mighty prince among us","A servant of the Most High","A friend of the king","A sojourner from Haran"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 23:6",verse:"Hear us, my lord: thou art a mighty prince among us: in the choice of our sepulchres bury thy dead; none of us shall withhold from thee his sepulchre, but that thou mayest bury thy dead.",insight:"Thou art a mighty prince among us. A quiet life of faith had earned the respect of watching neighbors; character preaches before we speak."},
{q:"What gesture did Abraham make before the people of the land?",options:["He bowed himself to the people of the land","He lifted his hands in prayer","He tore his garments","He fell on his face"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 23:7",verse:"And Abraham stood up, and bowed himself to the people of the land, even to the children of Heth.",insight:"He stood up and bowed. Courtesy and humility open doors that demands cannot; Abraham negotiated his grief with grace."},
{q:"To whom did Abraham ask the Hittites to speak for him?",options:["Ephron the son of Zohar","Abimelech the king","Mamre the Amorite","Phichol the captain"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 23:8",verse:"And he communed with them, saying, If it be your mind that I should bury my dead out of my sight; hear me, and intreat for me to Ephron the son of Zohar,",insight:"Intreat for me to Ephron the son of Zohar. He went through proper channels instead of seizing; faith is never careless with others' rights."},
{q:"Which cave did Abraham want to buy?",options:["The cave of Machpelah","The cave of Adullam","The cave of Makkedah","The cave of Engedi"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 23:9",verse:"That he may give me the cave of Machpelah, which he hath, which is in the end of his field; for as much money as it is worth he shall give it me for a possession of a buryingplace amongst you.",insight:"The cave of Machpelah, in the end of his field. Grief deserves its own ground; Abraham chose a specific place for a sacred purpose."},
{q:"Where exactly was the cave of Machpelah?",options:["In the end of Ephron's field","In the midst of the city","By the well of Beersheba","On the mount of Moriah"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 23:9",verse:"That he may give me the cave of Machpelah, which he hath, which is in the end of his field; for as much money as it is worth he shall give it me for a possession of a buryingplace amongst you.",insight:"In the end of his field, at the edge of things. That border cave would become the anchor tomb of a nation."},
{q:"What did Ephron first offer to do?",options:["Give Abraham the field and the cave freely","Sell it for a thousand shekels","Refuse to sell at all","Ask Abraham to leave the land"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 23:11",verse:"Nay, my lord, hear me: the field give I thee, and the cave that is therein, I give it thee; in the presence of the sons of my people give I it thee: bury thy dead.",insight:"The field give I thee, and the cave that is therein, I give it thee. Eastern courtesy offered it free; Abraham answered with integrity and insisted on paying."},
{q:"Before whom did Ephron make his offer to Abraham?",options:["In the audience of the children of Heth","In secret at night","Before the king only","Before Abraham's servants"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 23:10",verse:"And Ephron dwelt among the children of Heth: and Ephron the Hittite answered Abraham in the audience of the children of Heth, even of all that went in at the gate of his city, saying,",insight:"In the audience of the children of Heth, where all could hear. God's people deal in the open; witnesses make promises sure."},
{q:"How did Abraham answer Ephron's offer of a gift?",options:["He insisted on paying money for the field","He accepted it gladly","He offered half the price","He walked away from the deal"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 23:13",verse:"And he spake unto Ephron in the audience of the people of the land, saying, But if thou wilt give it, I pray thee, hear me: I will give thee money for the field; take it of me, and I will bury my dead there.",insight:"I will give thee money for the field; take it of me. The promise would not be built on charity; he paid the full price for his dead."},
{q:"What price did Ephron name for the land?",options:["Four hundred shekels of silver","A hundred pieces of gold","A thousand shekels of silver","Thirty pieces of silver"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 23:15",verse:"My lord, hearken unto me: the land is worth four hundred shekels of silver; what is that betwixt me and thee? bury therefore thy dead.",insight:"Four hundred shekels of silver; what is that betwixt me and thee? Polite words, full price. Abraham paid it all without haggling over his grief."},
{q:"How is the silver described that Abraham weighed out to Ephron?",options:["Current money with the merchant","Old coins of Egypt","Temple shekels","Unweighed lumps of metal"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 23:16",verse:"And Abraham hearkened unto Ephron; and Abraham weighed to Ephron the silver, which he had named in the audience of the sons of Heth, four hundred shekels of silver, current money with the merchant.",insight:"Current money with the merchant, weighed out honestly. Faith keeps clean books; even in mourning, Abraham dealt fairly."},
{q:"What was included in the purchase made sure to Abraham?",options:["The field, the cave, and all the trees in the field","Only the cave itself","The field and the city","The well and the grove"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 23:17",verse:"And the field of Ephron, which was in Machpelah, which was before Mamre, the field, and the cave which was therein, and all the trees that were in the field, that were in all the borders round about, were made sure",insight:"The field of Ephron, and the cave therein, and all the trees in the field, made sure. Every border marked; what God gives is sure and whole."},
{q:"Before whom was the purchase finalized?",options:["Before all that went in at the gate of his city","Before the priests alone","In Abraham's tent","At the well of Beersheba"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 23:18",verse:"Unto Abraham for a possession in the presence of the children of Heth, before all that went in at the gate of his city.",insight:"Before all that went in at the gate of his city. Public, witnessed, unshakable; the first deed of the promised land was signed at the city gate."},
{q:"Where did Abraham bury Sarah his wife?",options:["In the cave of the field of Machpelah before Mamre, that is Hebron","In Beersheba","Under the oaks of Mamre","In Haran"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 23:19",verse:"And after this, Abraham buried Sarah his wife in the cave of the field of Machpelah before Mamre: the same is Hebron in the land of Canaan.",insight:"He buried Sarah in the cave of Machpelah. Laid to rest in the land of promise, she waits there still for the resurrection morning."},
{q:"By whom was the field made sure to Abraham for a buryingplace?",options:["By the sons of Heth","By Abimelech","By the Amorites","By Pharaoh"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 23:20",verse:"And the field, and the cave that is therein, were made sure unto Abraham for a possession of a buryingplace by the sons of Heth.",insight:"By the sons of Heth it was made sure. Even strangers confirmed what God had given; heaven's deeds get earth's witnesses."},
{q:"What did this purchase become for Abraham's family?",options:["A possession of a buryingplace for generations","A pasture for his flocks","A marketplace","A fortress"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 23:20",verse:"And the field, and the cave that is therein, were made sure unto Abraham for a possession of a buryingplace by the sons of Heth.",insight:"A possession of a buryingplace. The first owned soil of Canaan was a grave, a down payment of resurrection hope in the land of promise."}
]},
{n:24, name:"Rebekah at the Well", seal:{ref:"Genesis 24:67",verse:"And Isaac brought her into his mother Sarah’s tent, and took Rebekah, and she became his wife; and he loved her: and Isaac was comforted after his mother’s death."}, facts:["Did you know the servant's prayer is one of the most specific prayers in Scripture? He asked God for a sign, and Rebekah appeared before he had finished speaking (Genesis 24:12-15).","Did you know watering ten camels was hours of hard labor? A thirsty camel drinks gallons, and Rebekah drew for every one of them by hand (Genesis 24:19-20).","Did you know Isaac was meditating in the field when Rebekah arrived? He went out at evening to think and pray, then lifted his eyes and saw the camels coming (Genesis 24:63)."], questions:[
{q:"How is Abraham described at the opening of the chapter?",options:["Old and well stricken in age, and the LORD had blessed him in all things","Young and strong","Sick and dying","Poor and afflicted"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 24:1",verse:"And Abraham was old, and well stricken in age: and the LORD had blessed Abraham in all things.",insight:"Old and well stricken in age, blessed in all things. A lifetime of blessing, yet one holy task remained: a wife for the son of promise."},
{q:"Which servant did Abraham charge with the mission?",options:["His eldest servant that ruled over all that he had","His youngest shepherd","A hired Canaanite","His armor bearer"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 24:2",verse:"And Abraham said unto his eldest servant of his house, that ruled over all that he had, Put, I pray thee, thy hand under my thigh:",insight:"The eldest servant that ruled over all that he had. The greatest trust went to the most proven hands; faithfulness in small things earns great errands."},
{q:"What sign of the oath did the servant perform?",options:["He put his hand under Abraham's thigh","He lifted his hand to heaven","He cut a covenant of animals","He swore by the altar"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 24:9",verse:"And the servant put his hand under the thigh of Abraham his master, and sware to him concerning that matter.",insight:"He put his hand under his master's thigh and sware. Solemn oaths for sacred errands; in Scripture, marriage is covenant business, never casual."},
{q:"From whom was the servant forbidden to take a wife for Isaac?",options:["The daughters of the Canaanites","The daughters of Egypt","The daughters of Heth","The daughters of Philistia"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 24:3",verse:"And I will make thee swear by the LORD, the God of heaven, and the God of the earth, that thou shalt not take a wife unto my son of the daughters of the Canaanites, among whom I dwell:",insight:"Not of the daughters of the Canaanites, among whom he dwelt. Faith seeks faith; the home you build shapes the heart you become."},
{q:"Where was the servant to find Isaac's wife?",options:["Abraham's country and kindred","The land of Egypt","The city of Gerar","The plains of Jordan"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 24:4",verse:"But thou shalt go unto my country, and to my kindred, and take a wife unto my son Isaac.",insight:"Unto my country and to my kindred. Back to the family of promise, not forward into Canaan's idols; direction matters in love."},
{q:"What did Abraham forbid the servant to do?",options:["Bring Isaac back to that land again","Take more than ten camels","Speak to Laban","Return without a wife"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 24:6",verse:"And Abraham said unto him, Beware thou that thou bring not my son thither again.",insight:"Beware thou that thou bring not my son thither again. Never go back; the promise moves forward, and so must the heir."},
{q:"Whom did Abraham say would go before the servant?",options:["The angel of the LORD","A guide from Haran","A pillar of cloud","One of his sons"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 24:7",verse:"The LORD God of heaven, which took me from my father’s house, and from the land of my kindred, and which spake unto me, and that sware unto me, saying, Unto thy seed will I give this land; he shall send his angel before thee, and thou shalt take a wife unto my son from thence.",insight:"He shall send his angel before thee. Heaven goes ahead of obedient errands; we walk into appointments God has already kept."},
{q:"How many camels did the servant take for the journey?",options:["Ten","Seven","Twelve","Forty"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 24:10",verse:"And the servant took ten camels of the camels of his master, and departed; for all the goods of his master were in his hand: and he arose, and went to Mesopotamia, unto the city of Nahor.",insight:"Ten camels, laden with all the goods of his master. God provides the means for His missions; the servant traveled like the wealth he represented."},
{q:"At what time did the servant reach the well outside the city?",options:["In the evening, when women go out to draw water","At noon","At sunrise","At midnight"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 24:11",verse:"And he made his camels to kneel down without the city by a well of water at the time of the evening, even the time that women go out to draw water.",insight:"At the time of the evening, even the time that women go out to draw water. God's timing often dresses itself in ordinary routine."},
{q:"What sign did the servant ask God to show him?",options:["The damsel who offers water to him and to his camels","A dove landing on the well","Thunder from a clear sky","A star standing over the city"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 24:14",verse:"And let it come to pass, that the damsel to whom I shall say, Let down thy pitcher, I pray thee, that I may drink; and she shall say, Drink, and I will give thy camels drink also: let the same be she that thou hast appointed for thy servant Isaac; and thereby shall I know that thou hast shewed kindness unto my master.",insight:"She that saith, Drink, and I will give thy camels drink also. He asked for kindness as the mark of God's choice; character outranks beauty."},
{q:"Who came out before the servant had finished praying?",options:["Rebekah, with her pitcher upon her shoulder","Laban with his flocks","Bethuel with his servants","An angel of the LORD"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 24:15",verse:"And it came to pass, before he had done speaking, that, behold, Rebekah came out, who was born to Bethuel, son of Milcah, the wife of Nahor, Abraham’s brother, with her pitcher upon her shoulder.",insight:"Before he had done speaking, Rebekah came out. God answers before we finish asking; heaven is never late to a prayed prayer."},
{q:"How is Rebekah described when she first appears?",options:["Very fair to look upon, a virgin","Old and wise","A widow in mourning","A queen in Egypt"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 24:16",verse:"And the damsel was very fair to look upon, a virgin, neither had any man known her: and she went down to the well, and filled her pitcher, and came up.",insight:"Very fair to look upon, a virgin, neither had any man known her. Beauty and purity together; God's gifts come whole, not divided."},
{q:"What did Rebekah do after giving the servant drink?",options:["She drew water for all his camels until they had done drinking","She ran to call her father","She asked for payment","She invited him to supper"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 24:19",verse:"And when she had done giving him drink, she said, I will draw water for thy camels also, until they have done drinking.",insight:"I will draw water for thy camels also, until they have done drinking. Generosity that goes the second mile; ten camels drink a great deal, and she drew it all."},
{q:"What did the servant do while watching her?",options:["He held his peace, wondering whether the LORD had prospered his journey","He immediately gave her the jewels","He ran back to the camels","He bowed and left"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 24:21",verse:"And the man wondering at her held his peace, to wit whether the LORD had made his journey prosperous or not.",insight:"The man wondering at her held his peace. Watch and wait before you declare; discernment tests the answer before announcing it."},
{q:"What gifts did the servant give Rebekah at the well?",options:["A golden earring and two bracelets of gold","A necklace of pearls","A crown of silver","A ring and a cloak"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 24:22",verse:"And it came to pass, as the camels had done drinking, that the man took a golden earring of half a shekel weight, and two bracelets for her hands of ten shekels weight of gold;",insight:"A golden earring of half a shekel weight, and bracelets of ten shekels. The bride adorned at the well, a picture of Christ adorning His church."},
{q:"Who was Rebekah's brother?",options:["Laban","Bethuel","Nahor","Huz"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 24:29",verse:"And Rebekah had a brother, and his name was Laban: and Laban ran out unto the man, unto the well.",insight:"Rebekah had a brother, and his name was Laban. Family ties that would shape Jacob's future too; God weaves generations together at wells."},
{q:"What did the servant refuse to do before telling his errand?",options:["Eat the meat set before him","Drink water","Enter the house","Sit at the table"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 24:33",verse:"And there was set meat before him to eat: but he said, I will not eat, until I have told mine errand. And he said, Speak on.",insight:"I will not eat, until I have told mine errand. God's business first; comfort can wait when the message is urgent."},
{q:"How did Laban and Bethuel answer the servant's story?",options:["The thing proceedeth from the LORD: we cannot speak unto thee bad or good","We must think on it for a year","Pay us a bride price first","She shall not go"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 24:50",verse:"Then Laban and Bethuel answered and said, The thing proceedeth from the LORD: we cannot speak unto thee bad or good.",insight:"The thing proceedeth from the LORD. When God is plainly in a thing, even hesitant hearts yield; providence persuades where arguments cannot."},
{q:"What was Rebekah's own answer when asked if she would go?",options:["I will go","Let me wait ten days","Ask my father first","I am afraid to go"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 24:58",verse:"And they called Rebekah, and said unto her, Wilt thou go with this man? And she said, I will go.",insight:"Wilt thou go with this man? And she said, I will go. She had never seen Isaac, yet she went; faith says yes before it sees."},
{q:"What comfort did Isaac find in Rebekah?",options:["He was comforted after his mother's death","He forgot the coming famine","He left Beersheba","He built an altar"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 24:67",verse:"And Isaac brought her into his mother Sarah’s tent, and took Rebekah, and she became his wife; and he loved her: and Isaac was comforted after his mother’s death.",insight:"He took Rebekah, and she became his wife; and he loved her: and Isaac was comforted after his mother's death. God heals grief with love; Sarah's tent was filled again."}
]},
{n:25, name:"Jacob and Esau", seal:{ref:"Genesis 25:23",verse:"And the LORD said unto her, Two nations are in thy womb, and two manner of people shall be separated from thy bowels; and the one people shall be stronger than the other people; and the elder shall serve the younger."}, facts:["Did you know Abraham lived a hundred and seventy five years? He died in a good old age, an old man, and full of years, and was gathered to his people (Genesis 25:7-8).","Did you know the name Edom means 'red'? Esau earned it from the red pottage he traded his birthright for, and his descendants were called Edomites (Genesis 25:30).","Did you know Ishmael had twelve princes, matching Israel's twelve tribes? God kept His promise to make a great nation of Abraham's other son too (Genesis 25:16)."], questions:[
{q:"Whom did Abraham take as wife after Sarah's death?",options:["Keturah","Hagar","Milcah","Reumah"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 25:1",verse:"Then again Abraham took a wife, and her name was Keturah.",insight:"Then again Abraham took a wife, and her name was Keturah. Life and fruitfulness continued; God's blessing overflowed beyond the promise line."},
{q:"How many sons did Keturah bear to Abraham?",options:["Six","Eight","Twelve","Three"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 25:2",verse:"And she bare him Zimran, and Jokshan, and Medan, and Midian, and Ishbak, and Shuah.",insight:"Zimran, Jokshan, Medan, Midian, Ishbak, and Shuah, six sons. The family widened, but the promise narrowed to Isaac; many children, one covenant."},
{q:"To whom did Abraham give all that he had?",options:["To Isaac","To Ishmael","To the sons of Keturah","To his eldest servant"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 25:5",verse:"And Abraham gave all that he had unto Isaac.",insight:"Abraham gave all that he had unto Isaac. The inheritance follows the promise, not birth order or affection; God's choosing settles the estate."},
{q:"What did Abraham do for the sons of his concubines?",options:["He gave them gifts and sent them eastward away from Isaac","He made them his heirs","He sold them into Egypt","He left them nothing"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 25:6",verse:"But unto the sons of the concubines, which Abraham had, Abraham gave gifts, and sent them away from Isaac his son, while he yet lived, eastward, unto the east country.",insight:"He gave them gifts and sent them away from Isaac his son, while he yet lived. Generosity with boundaries; the promise kept clear while love provided."},
{q:"How many years did Abraham live?",options:["A hundred and threescore and fifteen","A hundred and twenty seven","A hundred and eighty","Two hundred"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 25:7",verse:"And these are the days of the years of Abraham’s life which he lived, an hundred threescore and fifteen years.",insight:"A hundred and seventy five years. From Haran to Machpelah, every year a step of faith; a good old age is a finished journey, not merely a long one."},
{q:"Who buried Abraham?",options:["His sons Isaac and Ishmael","His servants","The sons of Heth","His nephews from Haran"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 25:9",verse:"And his sons Isaac and Ishmael buried him in the cave of Machpelah, in the field of Ephron the son of Zohar the Hittite, which is before Mamre;",insight:"His sons Isaac and Ishmael buried him. The divided brothers stood together at their father's grave; grace can reunite what rivalry tore apart."},
{q:"Where was Abraham buried?",options:["In the cave of Machpelah, with Sarah his wife","In Beersheba","In Haran","In the land of Egypt"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 25:10",verse:"The field which Abraham purchased of the sons of Heth: there was Abraham buried, and Sarah his wife.",insight:"In the field Abraham purchased, there was Abraham buried, and Sarah his wife. Rest beside Sarah in the purchased ground of promise, awaiting resurrection."},
{q:"Where did Isaac dwell after Abraham's death?",options:["By the well Lahairoi","In Hebron","In Gerar","In Bethel"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 25:11",verse:"And it came to pass after the death of Abraham, that God blessed his son Isaac; and Isaac dwelt by the well Lahai-roi.",insight:"Isaac dwelt by the well Lahairoi, the well of the God who sees me. Hagar's well of desperation became Isaac's home of blessing."},
{q:"Who was Ishmael's firstborn?",options:["Nebajoth","Kedar","Dumah","Tema"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 25:13",verse:"And these are the names of the sons of Ishmael, by their names, according to their generations: the firstborn of Ishmael, Nebajoth; and Kedar, and Adbeel, and Mibsam,",insight:"Nebajoth, named first among twelve. God kept His promise to make a nation of Ishmael, recording it name by name, heir by heir."},
{q:"How many princes came from Ishmael?",options:["Twelve","Seven","Ten","Seventy"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 25:16",verse:"These are the sons of Ishmael, and these are their names, by their towns, and by their castles; twelve princes according to their nations.",insight:"Twelve princes according to their nations. Twelve princes for Ishmael, twelve tribes for Isaac; God keeps His word to both sons of Abraham."},
{q:"How long did Ishmael live?",options:["A hundred and thirty seven years","A hundred and seventy five years","A hundred and twenty years","Ninety years"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 25:17",verse:"And these are the years of the life of Ishmael, an hundred and thirty and seven years: and he gave up the ghost and died; and was gathered unto his people.",insight:"A hundred and thirty seven years. His years were numbered too; the God who heard the lad in the wilderness kept him all his days."},
{q:"How old was Isaac when he took Rebekah to wife?",options:["Forty years old","Thirty years old","Sixty years old","Twenty five years old"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 25:20",verse:"And Isaac was forty years old when he took Rebekah to wife, the daughter of Bethuel the Syrian of Padan-aram, the sister to Laban the Syrian.",insight:"Isaac was forty years old when he took Rebekah. He waited, he prayed, and God gave; the son of laughter learned patience before fatherhood."},
{q:"Why did Isaac entreat the LORD for his wife?",options:["Because she was barren","Because she was sick","Because of the famine","Because of Esau"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 25:21",verse:"And Isaac intreated the LORD for his wife, because she was barren: and the LORD was intreated of him, and Rebekah his wife conceived.",insight:"Isaac intreated the LORD for his wife, because she was barren. The pattern repeats: barrenness met by prayer, promise met by miracle."},
{q:"What did Rebekah do when the children struggled together within her?",options:["She went to enquire of the LORD","She sent for her mother","She wept alone","She asked Isaac to pray"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 25:22",verse:"And the children struggled together within her; and she said, If it be so, why am I thus? And she went to enquire of the LORD.",insight:"If it be so, why am I thus? And she went to enquire of the LORD. Take your turmoil to God; He answers confusion with truth."},
{q:"What did the LORD tell Rebekah about her sons?",options:["Two nations are in thy womb, and the elder shall serve the younger","Both shall be shepherds","The younger shall die young","They shall dwell in peace forever"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 25:23",verse:"And the LORD said unto her, Two nations are in thy womb, and two manner of people shall be separated from thy bowels; and the one people shall be stronger than the other people; and the elder shall serve the younger.",insight:"The elder shall serve the younger. God's choosing, not man's ordering; grace elects before birth, and the promise runs by mercy, not merit."},
{q:"How is Esau described at his birth?",options:["Red, all over like a hairy garment","Fair and smooth","Small and weak","Dark as night"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 25:25",verse:"And the first came out red, all over like an hairy garment; and they called his name Esau.",insight:"The first came out red, all over like an hairy garment. Marked from birth, the red hunter already showing his color; they called his name Esau."},
{q:"What did Jacob's hand do at his birth?",options:["It took hold on Esau's heel","It reached for his mother","It grasped a cloth","It waved in the air"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 25:26",verse:"And after that came his brother out, and his hand took hold on Esau’s heel; and his name was called Jacob: and Isaac was threescore years old when she bare them.",insight:"His hand took hold on Esau's heel, and his name was called Jacob. The heel grasper, striving from the womb; God would wrestle him into Israel."},
{q:"How did the brothers differ as they grew?",options:["Esau was a cunning hunter, Jacob a plain man dwelling in tents","Both were shepherds","Esau was a farmer, Jacob a hunter","Both dwelt in tents"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 25:27",verse:"And the boys grew: and Esau was a cunning hunter, a man of the field; and Jacob was a plain man, dwelling in tents.",insight:"Esau was a cunning hunter, a man of the field; Jacob was a plain man, dwelling in tents. Different gifts, different callings; weigh the hearts, not the hobbies."},
{q:"What did Esau sell his birthright for?",options:["Bread and pottage of lentils","A flock of sheep","A field in Canaan","A bag of silver"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 25:34",verse:"Then Jacob gave Esau bread and pottage of lentiles; and he did eat and drink, and rose up, and went his way: thus Esau despised his birthright.",insight:"Jacob gave Esau bread and pottage of lentiles. The eternal traded for the immediate; appetite makes a poor bargainer, and hunger a worse counselor."},
{q:"How does Scripture sum up Esau's choice?",options:["Thus Esau despised his birthright","Thus Esau was blessed","Thus Esau repented","Thus Esau was forgiven"],a:0,ref:"Genesis 25:34",verse:"Then Jacob gave Esau bread and pottage of lentiles; and he did eat and drink, and rose up, and went his way: thus Esau despised his birthright.",insight:"Thus Esau despised his birthright. One line, a lifetime's warning: he ate and drank, and rose up, and went his way, despising the sacred for the stomach."}
]}
]);
